LightGBM shows a larger train to hold-out gap ({gap_l:.3f} against {gap_s:.3f}), so it is more prone to overfit. Calibration, stress and out-of-time results are left to the independent validation.

## 8. Assumptions and known limitations
1. Relationships learned in 1999-2004 (a benign period) hold in other regimes; the crisis test challenges this.
2. Sample files only; about {bads_train:,} bad loans in training, thin for tree models.
3. Accepted-only population, no reject inference.
4. State is a feature and may proxy for geography-related risk; it needs fairness review.
5. Some bins are tiny (smallest retained: {tiny_feat} = {tiny_bin}, {tiny_n} loans), so estimates there are unreliable.
6. No macroeconomic variables, so the models cannot respond to the cycle.
7. Credit score has unusually high information value ({iv_fico:.2f}); treat it as a concentration risk.

